    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-ceiling utility of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (78.75) and the late-season surge of **Kyle Tucker** (77.19). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against the left-handed Basso, with park factors providing a significant 10% boost to his outlook. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** remains our premier weapon despite a potential lineup shift, as his efficiency against Rhett Lowder\u2019s 4.82 xERA makes him an essential start. We are also leaning heavily on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.55), who draws a prime matchup against the vulnerable Sugano; the combination of a 4.87 xERA and a dynamic platoon advantage makes him our highest-scoring middle infielder today.\n\nStrategic attention turns to the outfield and third base, where **Coby Mayo** (66.71) is a standout play. His score is bolstered by a 16% park factor uplift and favorable wind conditions, which outweigh the minor penalty from the opposing catcher's pop time. **Henry Bolte** (60.78) also cracked our recommended start threshold, as his leadoff placement and park factors mitigate the risk of facing the right-handed Fisher. Conversely, the bench remains thin due to the ongoing absences of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg**, all of whom remain on the IL. **Jackson Merrill** (57.91) sits on the cusp of our \"Strong\" tier; he just missed the higher bucket due to the platoon disadvantage against the left-handed Kent, but he remains our most viable option to fill the final outfield slot ahead of organizational depth pieces like **Wade Meckler** or **Luis Lara**.\n\nRisk management remains a priority for our middle-infield rotation. While **Nasim Nunez** (54.50) is starting, he is clearly near the floor of our acceptable range; his score is hampered by a significant negative adjustment for his #8 batting order position. We are monitoring **Kyle Tucker** closely, as his \"Lineup Pending\" status necessitates a secondary plan should he receive a rest day. As we navigate the stretch run, we will continue to prioritize the speed tools of **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** to maintain our competitive edge in the scarcity-driven SB category, even as we temper expectations for their overall offensive output against elite arms like Buehler.",
